With the same vision backbone, our ST augmentation outperforms the spatiotemporal descriptors (STD) of OST and class-level prompts (CT) on all three datasets (Table~\ref{tab:ep2}; e.g., UCF101 85.2 vs.\ 84.9 vs.\ 83.8).

\subsection{Ablation and Analysis}
\input{tables/table_vi}
\paragraph{STCA.} On UCF101 (EP3), frozen CLIP reaches 74.2 (Table~\ref{tab:ab1}). Prompt-based adaptation with MCM improves it by up to 8.5 points (82.7). Full tuning with MCM only gives 84.6 (+10.4), and WSM+MCM with continual mixing gives 85.2 (+11.0). WSM and MCM are thus complementary, and continual mixing is slightly better than separate mixing.

